1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Just where do you think you're running off to, Beta?

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
What was that?

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Icarus, what's the matter?

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Nothing.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Gamma!

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
You got it. We're the Angeloid Interceptors. Type Gamma and Type Harpy.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
It's the Uranus Queen Swanson. We're here to take the bitch down.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Don't you worry about a thing. You see, Master asked us to do this.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
I'll bet you didn't know he's been watching over you this entire time.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Actually, he's been quite worried about you.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
He's worried about me?

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Well, he did tell you to take on the Uranus Queen by yourself.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
And that's a hell of a tall order for anyone, even one of us.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
When he realized you might get hurt attempting it, he acted quickly to mount a rescue.

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,000
He sent us here to bring you home as soon as possible.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Sounds like Master's pretty lonely without you up there with him, Beta.

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Master's worried about me. And he's actually lonely without me, too. I never expected that.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:35,000
As much as she enjoys hanging around those insects, this must be torturing her.

19
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:41,000
She'll destroy the Uranus Queen, kill the humans, and then return to me, filled with joy.

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Certain I'm going to applaud what a good job she did.

21
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
And that's the moment I'll tell the wretched thing.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
It's time to send your ass to the scrapyard.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,000
I can't wait to see the horrified face she makes when I drop that bomb on her.

24
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:13,000
There is no more time.

25
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Hear me. You must save the angel, please.

26
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
She is being held by the sky.

27
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
That same weird-ass dream again.

28
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Are you finally waking up, Master?

29
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Yeah. Where's Nymph?

30
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Well, she's...

31
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,000
What? Are you serious? Nymph pulled another disappearing act?

32
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Correct. This is becoming something of a pattern.

33
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
She's making me crazy. What's her deal?

34
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Like Icarus said, she's always taking off.

35
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Come on, you have to have some idea why, Tomaki.

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Did you do something bad to her? It wouldn't be the first time you did something dumb.

37
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
What are you...

38
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Whoa, no. I didn't do anything wrong, okay? We're cool.

39
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Are you sure?

40
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Because the look on your face says the exact opposite of the words coming out of your mouth.

41
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Stop reading into it. It's nothing. Leave me alone.

42
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Come to think of it, I did see Nymph flying toward the forest last night.

43
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
At the time, it didn't seem that odd.

44
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
You mean it?

45
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:26,000
But now that I think back, she might have been fretting over something. Or I could be wrong.

46
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Well, maybe we should go out and look for her, don't you think?

47
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
She can't miss our Christmas party tonight.

48
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
I'm not worried about it. She came back last time she did this.

49
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Let's just focus on setting up the party. We'll wait for her if we have to.

50
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Then how about we go find a tree for this shindig? It's one of the big things we're missing.

51
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
And speaking of big, I have to say I am partial to the large ones.

52
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
You got any idea where we can find a big one?

53
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
I actually know of an excellent spot to look.

54
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
There's an ideal tree near the riverbed next to my place.

55
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
That's great. But do you have something to chop it down with?

56
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
I'm just saying if you don't, you could always borrow my axe.

57
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
No problem there. I have the perfect axe for chopping wood.

58
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
I'll leave the rest of this to you.

59
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
See you in a little bit.

60
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
That's amazing. You're fast.

61
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
No, wait! Stop!

62
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Icarus, you're whipping too fast now! You have to stop it!

63
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Alright.

64
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Oh, man.

65
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
You charred the bowl.

66
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
I have failed.

67
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Oh, no worries. We're still having fun, right?

68
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Just us girls making a cake together, finally having some bonding time?

69
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
I just wish Nymph could be here to enjoy it all with us.

70
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
What is that?

71
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Oh, yeah. I brought it thinking we could use some of these pictures to decorate for the party.

72
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Brings back some fun memories, huh?

73
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:06,000
We've done so much in the short amount of time we've known each other.

74
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Yeah, but this one right here is my favorite of the bunch.

75
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
When we first met, I never imagined you and I would hit it off as well as we have.

76
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
But I'm glad we did.

77
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Perfect. Seems the information you gave us was accurate. This is an excellent location. No place for her to hide. And we've got a great vantage point.

78
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:48,000
We shall be proceeding as planned.

79
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Starting from here on out, we're going to need you to hide us with your P-Stone system. That's our best angle of attack. Don't worry. When you need help, we'll back you up.

80
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Back me up?

81
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:08,000
That's right. With our super hot compressed projectile cannon, Prometheus. It fires vaporized matter heated to 3,000 degrees Celsius at 4 kilometers a second.

82
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:15,000
If she doesn't have the time to deploy Aegis, the Uranus Queen will be no different than any of us in a battle. We'll get her in one shot.

83
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Hold on! I thought the orders Master gave her for the two of you to bring her back in one piece, not destroy her! In fact, I thought you were supposed to tug her into returning!

84
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Well, that's true. But we do have to protect ourselves if things don't go according to plan. Still gotta cover our asses, don't we?

85
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:36,000
We need you to do everything you can to keep us from having to use these dangerous toys.

86
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:44,000
It'll be fine. I'm sure you'll be able to do a great job convincing her. This is just insurance.

87
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:51,000
All that we do here is for our Master. If you succeed, he will have great cause to rejoice. Don't you think?

88
00:06:51,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Master will be happy with me then. I understand. But promise me you won't interfere until I finish trying to persuade her.

89
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Oh, sure. Of course we won't.

90
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:24,000
I can't help but wonder what your true Master would think if you learned what you were doing here.

91
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Little Miss Weapon of DEATH!

92
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
What? What are you doing?

93
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Look, Nymph. The sky here is so vast.

94
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:43,000
It's true. Angeloids aren't designed to smile. Not unless we have humans around to help us learn.

95
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:53,000
This cage is like our chokers. If that's true, they want out.

96
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
They want out.

97
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Hey, where are you going?

98
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,000
I just need to go get something I forgot.

99
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Why don't you just give Tomaki a call? He's already out picking up things for the party.

100
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Oh, no. I'll just...

101
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Icarus, remember you promised you wouldn't lie anymore. You don't have to.

102
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:34,000
You're surrounded by your friends here. You can talk to us about anything. You know that, don't you?

103
00:08:34,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Anyway, the cake will be out of the oven soon. So, hurry back.

104
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Hurry back.

105
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Icarus, what you doing? Did you come down here to pick me up?

106
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Icarus, what you doing? Did you come down here to pick me up?

107
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Icarus, what you doing?

108
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,860
Did you come down here to pick me up?

109
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:32,840
Awesome, perfect timing.

110
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,760
You can help me carry one of these bags.

111
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:36,120
I got a whole bunch of stuff.

112
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:38,840
Party poppers, tinsel, way more than we need.

113
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:41,040
Master?

114
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:42,640
Oh, wait, you're gonna freak.

115
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:43,780
Check this out.

116
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:45,460
Isn't this hilarious?

117
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:47,520
Stupid, creepy Santa mask.

118
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:51,240
Master.

119
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:53,340
Come on, you gotta try it on.

120
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,340
Just for a sec.

121
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,060
That looks kick-ass.

122
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:05,180
Goodbye.

123
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:11,920
I've come to tell you goodbye.

124
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,780
I know our time together was short.

125
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:18,980
And I apologize for all the trouble I've caused you.

126
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,420
But Master?

127
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:22,560
Master?

128
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:25,000
I will never forget you.

129
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:26,400
I promise.

130
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,340
These memories...

131
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:31,240
I'm going to keep them forever.

132
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:33,600
Wait, what the hell?

133
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:37,080
Is this your attempt at making a joke?

134
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,340
Look, Icarus...

135
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:44,820
I love you, Master.

136
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,720
And I always have over...

137
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:57,100
Goodbye.

138
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:57,780
Goodbye.

139
00:10:57,780 --> 00:10:58,280
Goodbye.

140
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,000
Goodbye.

141
00:10:59,000 --> 00:10:59,380
Goodbye.

142
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:01,980
Goodbye.

143
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:02,400
Goodbye.

144
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:05,460
Goodbye.

145
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,220
Goodbye.

146
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:08,940
Goodbye.

147
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:09,680
Goodbye.

148
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:10,200
Goodbye.

149
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:10,680
Goodbye.

150
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:10,920
Goodbye.

151
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:11,340
Goodbye.

152
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:11,960
Goodbye.

153
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:12,560
Goodbye.

154
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:12,700
Goodbye.

155
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:13,060
Goodbye.

156
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:13,160
Goodbye.

157
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:26,300
TARGEOUS

158
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:49,480
That had to have been caused by some kind of attack from the sky.

159
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,320
Beginning data scan of the impact crater.

160
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:59,120
Analysis indicates Interceptor-class Angeloids, type Gamma and type Harpy.

161
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:01,960
That's Nymph signal.

162
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:08,400
But most likely I am your target.

163
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:12,940
I will have to fight them, as the Weapon Master hates so much.

164
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,820
I can't go back to him anymore.

165
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:18,740
I won't ever see him again.

166
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:22,920
Goodbye? That's crap.

167
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,360
Wow, it's huge!

168
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:28,460
We couldn't find the perfect tree, so we settled on this one.

169
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:32,080
Mikiko's heart was set on a big tree, so that's precisely what we got.

170
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:32,980
Is Icarus here?

171
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:33,580
Tomo!

172
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:33,920
Guys!

173
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,340
Wait, Tomo! Where are you going?

174
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:49,860
First Icarus and Nymph show up out of nowhere, and then they just vanish.

175
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:53,560
Did they even consider the fact that I might be worried about them?

176
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,680
That's why I didn't want to live with them.

177
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,440
Because I knew I'd get attached.

178
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:01,580
If they're gone, I guess at least I'd get my peace and quiet back.

179
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,680
I mean, that's all I ever really wanted, right?

180
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,100
That's why I didn't want to live with them.

181
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:21,900
I'm sorry, Alpha, but I had to get you along for a minute to talk.

182
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:26,560
I've kept quiet about it since I showed up.

183
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:30,760
But the real reason I'm here is to take you back to the sky, of course.

184
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,380
Okay, then.

185
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:37,440
So, you've known?

186
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:59,400
Why am I even looking for them?

187
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:05,260
Sorry to keep you waiting, Tomoki.

188
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:07,900
Sugata, why are you here?

189
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:10,320
You're looking for Icarus and Nymph, aren't you?

190
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:15,540
According to the eyewitness reports I've gathered from the area,

191
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:17,260
she shouldn't have gone too far from here.

192
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:21,380
Judging by her direction, airspeed, and abilities,

193
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:24,240
I think it'd be best if we were to search this area here.

194
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:25,740
But if so...

195
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,080
I know exactly what's going through that brain of yours.

196
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:30,540
Hop on. I'll give you a pump.

197
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:33,440
That's not exactly fair.

198
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:37,360
You're running off to do all the cool stuff without me.

199
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:45,040
Why?

200
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,060
Why?

201
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:51,080
I said why!

202
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:52,460
What are you doing?

203
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:55,500
You said you'd let me try to convince her.

204
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:58,080
Why did you just attack her out of nowhere?

205
00:14:58,500 --> 00:14:58,760
Huh.

206
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:00,040
You're such an idiot.

207
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:00,800
We lied.

208
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,780
Idiot or not, she helped us do this without much effort.

209
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:05,620
Good point.

210
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:07,540
Guess we should say thanks, Nymph.

211
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:09,340
We've got a lot on our plate.

212
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:10,480
Appreciate the shortcut.

213
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,080
What are you talking about?

214
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,180
What about Master?

215
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,640
We're here for one thing.

216
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:17,600
We need to collect her Uranus System Core,

217
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:19,200
the Variable Wings.

218
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:21,840
Master asked us to bring that back.

219
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:22,720
And only that.

220
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,840
Thanks for taking time to play with us, Nymph.

221
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:26,180
But you told me...

222
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:27,680
And now we're finished with you.

223
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:28,740
Get lost.

224
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,220
Please, don't do this.

225
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:37,840
Yeah, this was just way too easy.

226
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,680
Bye-bye, Uranus Queen.

227
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:41,960
Stop it!

228
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:44,340
Tomuki would never get over this.

229
00:15:44,340 --> 00:16:14,160
No, I want you to stay here.

230
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,120
Not gonna happen.

231
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:15,920
I'm going with you.

232
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:16,620
You can't.

233
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:17,580
We're going to...

234
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:19,020
And there's a Nymph for my friends too.

235
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:20,940
It doesn't matter if you like it or not.

236
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,540
If you don't take me with you,

237
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:23,900
I'll karate chop you.

238
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:26,220
And I won't stop till you're dead.

239
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:29,420
Zahara.

240
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:35,080
You got ruined.

241
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,700
You're in pieces.

242
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:36,760
Nymph.

243
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:58,660
Hey, what's with the banners?

244
00:16:58,660 --> 00:17:00,500
They were Zahara's idea.

245
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:02,460
Let's see.

246
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:05,200
Happy birthday, Icarus and Nymph?

247
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:07,640
Do Angeloids even have birthdays?

248
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,220
I don't know.

249
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:11,100
I asked them and they said they didn't.

250
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:13,520
So I talked about it with Sugata and Prez

251
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:15,500
and we decided to give them one.

252
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,800
I suppose it makes sense for Christmas

253
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,220
to be the birthday for angels.

254
